From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: ucsi: Restore the USB data check on partner change

Commit 0c8ee850572b ("usb: typec: ucsi: Add UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB quirk
for X1E80100") was meant to let USB4 partners keep their role on
platforms with the UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB quirk. Instead, the check in
ucsi_partner_change() that sets the role to USB_ROLE_NONE when the
partner does not support USB data now only applies on those platforms.
Everywhere else the role follows the partner type, even for a partner
without USB data and after a disconnect, while ucsi_register_port()
still applies the original check.

So on platforms with a USB role switch and without the quirk, a partner
without USB data, such as a charger, now changes the controller's role.
This was found on a Huawei Matebook E Go with usb_0 set up as dual-role,
as an Android port of the tablet does (upstream it is host-only): its EC
reports partner type UFP in every connector status, even with nothing
attached, and never sets the USB flag. Every connect and disconnect
switched the dwc3 controller to host mode, and a computer the tablet was
plugged into no longer saw it.

Apply the USB data check on all platforms again, and keep the USB4
exception for platforms with the quirk.

Fixes: 0c8ee850572b ("usb: typec: ucsi: Add UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB quirk for X1E80100")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
index c145063..9c4eaf4 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi.c
@@ -1367,10 +1367,14 @@ static void ucsi_partner_change(struct ucsi_connector *con)
 			typec_partner_set_usb_mode(con->partner, USB_MODE_USB4);
 	}
 
-	if ((!UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB)) &&
-	    ((con->ucsi->quirks & UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB) &&
-	     (!(UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN3) ||
-		UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN4)))))
+	/*
+	 * Only notify USB controller if partner supports USB data. With
+	 * UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB, a USB4 partner counts as supporting it.
+	 */
+	if (!UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB) &&
+	    !((con->ucsi->quirks & UCSI_USB4_IMPLIES_USB) &&
+	      (UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN3) ||
+	       UCSI_CONSTAT(con, PARTNER_FLAG_USB4_GEN4))))
 		u_role = USB_ROLE_NONE;
 
 	ret = usb_role_switch_set_role(con->usb_role_sw, u_role);
